{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Generally, no. In ordinary dealing, a US ’40 Act ETF issues and redeems shares directly with the fund only in large blocks called **creation units**, and only through authorized participants (typically broker-dealers). Retail investors ordinarily can’t redeem individual shares with the fund.\n\nInstead, they buy and sell ETF shares on an exchange through a broker, at market prices that may differ slightly from the ETF’s net asset value."}}
